# launch.conf: the windows launch-desktop opens at login. No AI is called.
# Copy to ~/.config/quantum-kittens/launch.conf and edit it there.
#
# One window per line:   name   check   command
#   check    process name to look for; if it is already running in a
#            terminal (or, for an app, at all) the line is skipped.
#            "-" means the command itself refuses to open a second copy.
#   command  runs in a new terminal window. Start it with @ for an app
#            that opens its own window.
#
# Comment out a seat that is paused or out of usage. Opening an agent's
# window does not start a turn, but notes waiting for it will be pasted in
# once it is idle.
#
# Written by: Claude (2026-11-25)

# The command deck: fullscreen on workspace 5, and half on workspace 1.
chat-full   -          @comms-deck-chat
chat-half   -          @comms-deck-chat half

# The navigation deck: seats, usage, workspaces and machine vitals,
# fullscreen on workspace 2 (Written by: vibe, 2026-11-26).
nav-full    -          @navigation-deck-chat

# Terminal seats.
grok        grok       grok
claude      claude     claude
vibe        vibe-rs    vibe
#gravity    agy        agy
#codex      codex      codex

# App seats.
grok-bot    grok-bot   @grok-bot
#lumo       lumo-desktop  @lumo-desktop
